# SysML Parallel TVCache — project agent rules

Learned from CURSOR_HANDOFF.md, m4999 smoke evidence, and Gary's characterization workflow.

## Deployment boundaries

- NERSC is inference-only. Harbor / Pi / task / verifier run on the Mac via Docker.
- Use only m4999 GPU credits (`--account=m4999 --constraint=gpu`). Never fall back to ntrain5.
- Proven allocation shape: 1 GPU, 32 CPUs, 56G, `shared_interactive`. Smoke ≤20 minutes; characterization campaigns may use up to QOS MaxWall (4h). Request once; release promptly.
- Preserve FlashInfer workaround until retested: node-local JIT caches and `VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_SAMPLER=0`.
- Valid vLLM flag: `--default-chat-template-kwargs` (not `--chat-template-kwargs`).
- For Qwen3.5 multimodal checkpoints on text-only DeepSWE: always pass `--language-model-only` (and `--reasoning-parser qwen3` when using thinking-off). Without it, encoder init can hang after weight load.

## Evidence honesty

- Reward 0 with `exception_info=null` is a correctly graded unsuccessful task, not infrastructure success by itself.
- A numeric reward alone does not prove agent execution succeeded; inspect Pi session, backend status, and verifier.
- Report observed lack of tool calls / parallel calls honestly. Do not force tool calls or alter tasks to manufacture parallelism.
- Preserve existing `results/` and `jobs/` evidence. Do not delete during cleanup. Do not commit secrets from `.local-smoke/`.

## Characterization conventions

- Characterization does not depend on Rust TVCache integration.
- Current turn = each saved assistant message, including valid zero-call turns.
- Overall parallel-turn fraction = turns with >1 emitted call / all assistant turns.
- Per-tool rows count that tool's calls over the same all-turn denominator; a read+bash turn is not a multi-read turn. Label this explicitly.
- Use an explicit campaign manifest for run selection. Do not glob all of `jobs/` as a clean dataset.
- Pi `tool_execution_start` events are not actual execute overlap; instrument execute entry/exit later.
- Cache integration is later work; uncached pilots use `hit=false` / `cache_mode=none`.
- Stock-image A arms (9B/4B × t8/t50 on unmodified DeepSWE; ~0–1.7% parallel) are **infra / early evidence only**. Handout DeepSWE requires **setup-as-agent-actions** variants (`scripts/prepare_task.py --setup-as-agent-actions` → `variants/deep-swe-setup/tasks/`). Re-run characterization on those variants before claiming the handout A cell; then B on the **same** variants. Do not block on 113-task sweeps or MLX parity.
- Never edit official `vendor/deep-swe/tasks/` in place for setup variants. Agent env: thin base image + setup preamble; verifier/tests stay authoritative (often still FROM the prebuilt swe-bench image). Agent network may be `public`/`allowlist` for clone/install; verifier stays `no-network`.
- Crystal-clear TVCache opportunity surfaces (Gary 2026-10-30):
  1. **Key = trajectory prefix in the Tool Call Graph**, not “same command string.” Same bash text after a different mutating prefix is a **different** node (correct miss).
  2. **Paper training win = cross-rollout reuse:** R parallel rollouts of the **same task** share one TCG. Rollout 2 hits paths rollout 1 already executed. Calls need not be in the same turn. Multi-tool-in-one-turn is **not** required for this win.
  3. **Single cold rollout / single attempt with empty cache:** first walk of each path is a **miss**. Later turns in that same rollout only hit if they repeat the **same stateful prefix + call** (uncommon for mutating chains; possible for repeated reads at unchanged state). Expecting high hit rate from one cold DeepSWE attempt alone is the wrong mental model.
  4. **Within-turn N>1 tools:** calls are **siblings under the same pre-turn stateful prefix**, not a forced chain. C needs batch lookup/partial hit/call-IDs (+ in-flight lease if two attempts miss the same path together). Not fuzzy matching. Storage options: per-call under shared prefix, whole-turn entry, or hybrid (handout compare).
  5. **Course A metric** (parallel-turn fraction) measures multi-call-turn prevalence only. It is not the paper’s cross-rollout hit-rate story.
  6. **Course B/C hit rates in eval** require shared/warm TCG across pass@k (or concurrent) attempts. Inference is the assigned testbed (handout: no training); the same C mechanics apply harder in GRPO’s R parallel rollouts.
- Low observed parallel-turn % is valid A evidence. Report honestly; do not prompt-hack tasks to manufacture parallelism for A tables. Teammate MLX ~48% is a different cell, not a reason to reopen A as critical path.

## Dual-model comparison (team split)

- Gary: `Qwen/Qwen3.5-9B` on NERSC (m4999) + Mac Harbor/Pi.
- Teammate: Qwen3-4B-Instruct locally.
- Hold constant: Harbor/Pi harness version, task ids/variants, grading, cache mode (`none` for characterization), and analysis denominators.
- Vary: model only. Report parallel-turn fraction and calls-per-turn CDF **per model** as well as pooled, and state whether tool-call patterns differ a lot.
- Agree the shared task list and attempt budget before scaling either side. Do not silently diverge on prompts, max_turns, thinking mode, or task variants.
- Teammate PDF rankings from TVCache/MLX/`1 trial × 8 steps` are **not** Harbor/Pi cells. Ablate with Harbor/Pi arms in `configs/ablation-model-steps-v1.md` (`9b-t8`, `4b-t8`, `4b-t50`). Confirm DeepSWE `git rev-parse HEAD` with teammate; task-id set is 113 and overlaps, but commit/image pins may still differ.
- Live runs need a fresh NERSC `sshproxy` cert (≈24h). Agent sandboxes cannot refresh MFA or access Metal for local MLX; run those in the user’s Terminal.
- Ablation Harbor loops must run under `bash` (scripts with `#!/usr/bin/env bash`). Inline zsh treats arrays as 1-indexed and empties `need[0]`, producing bogus job names like `abl-*-a`.
- Durable Mac runners: prefer `screen -dmS … bash scripts/…` over Cursor-shell `nohup`; the agent sandbox can kill detached jobs and blocks `ps`/`kill` of other PIDs. Keep using Harbor `jobs/` as primary evidence.
- `abl-9b-t8v4` (9B @ max_turns=8, 3×5) finished with usable Pi sessions on one 45m m4999 serve: parallel **1/63 = 1.59%** (one actionlint turn with 3 calls). Comparable to 9B@50 baseline 1.67%.
- `abl-4b-t8v1` (4B-Instruct-2507 @ max_turns=8, 3×5, hermes parser): parallel **0/67 = 0.00%**. Model id must stay `Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507` unless teammate confirms otherwise.
- `abl-4b-t50v1` (same 4B @ max_turns=50, 3×5): parallel **0/95 = 0.00%**. Finished in ~51m on one alloc; `scancel` immediately on DONE.
- Batched restart remains the safety net if EngineDead returns; unset stale `SYSML_JOB_PREFIX` before switching arms so need[] does not skip under the wrong wave.
- Protect m4999 hours: poll every few minutes during live serves; `scancel` immediately on backend death, Harbor stall (~12 min no session progress and no env/verifier container), or arm completion. Never leave a ready vLLM idle while the Mac runner is dead.

## Trace retention (Harbor-native is primary)

- Every attempt must keep the **standard Harbor trial directory** under `jobs/<job-name>/<task_id>__<suffix>/`.
- Required artifacts: `result.json`, `agent/pi/sessions/*.jsonl`, `verifier/reward.json`, and patch under `artifacts/` when present. Prefer also `agent/trajectory.json` / `agent/pi.txt`.
- Do not discard or overwrite prior trials; use a unique `--job-name` / jobs subdir per campaign wave.
- Prefer short `--job-name` prefixes and `k=1` loops over `k=5` in one Harbor invocation on Docker Desktop: long `jobs/<wave>-<task>/<task>__suffix/...` bind paths can race (`bind source path does not exist`). Agent-phase traces still count for characterization if verifier build fails; mark verifier failures explicitly and do not invent rewards.
- Harbor/verifier builds: set `DOCKER_BUILDKIT=0` / `COMPOSE_DOCKER_CLI_BUILD=0` when buildx fails with `operation not permitted` on `~/.docker/buildx/refs` temp files. Classic builder works for DeepSWE verifier Dockerfiles.
- Normalized CSV/manifest exports are secondary aids for aggregation. Re-derive counts from Harbor Pi session JSONL when in doubt.
- `cache_mode=none` for characterization; record model id, task, attempt index, and Harbor/Pi versions in the campaign manifest that points at these Harbor paths.

## Model changes

- Do not blindly rename the model in one file. Update sbatch helper, gateway `--model`, `SYSML_MODEL_ID`, LoopbackPi probe/limits, and Harbor `-m` together.
- Installed remote stack: vLLM 0.31.0. `Qwen/Qwen3.5-9B` needs a Qwen3.5-capable vLLM (tool parser `qwen3_coder`; prefer `--language-model-only` for text DeepSWE). Validate/upgrade before GPU spend.
- `Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B` remains deferred until that newer stack is proven.

## Placeholders the human must fill

Any live run needs fresh values for: SSH proxy freshness, `SYSML_REMOTE_ROOT`, Slurm account, `SYSML_ALLOC_NODE`, tunnel ports, gateway volume name, compose overlay path, gateway env file, job name, and model records directory. Historical nid/volume/port names from prior jobs are provenance only.

## Sharing

- Never share `.local-smoke/`, `.env`, `jobs/`, or raw `results/` wholesale.
- Teammate pack: `bash scripts/pack_team_share.sh`. See `docs/TEAM_SHARE.md`.

## Canonical TVCache references

- Paper (ICML 2026): *TVCACHE: A Stateful Tool-Value Cache for Post-Training LLM Agents* — [arXiv:2602.10986](https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.10986) ([PDF](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2602.10986), [HTML](https://arxiv.org/html/2602.10986), [slides](https://icml.cc/media/icml-2026/Slides/61148.pdf)). Authors include Abhishek Vijaya Kumar + Bhaskar Kataria (Cornell).
- Assigned stack already vendored: `vendor/tvcache-rust/` (cache server, TCP `:7878`) and `vendor/tvclient/` (Python client / `TvcacheToolExecutor`). Upstream: https://github.com/abhivijay96/tvcache-rust , https://github.com/abhivijay96/tvclient . Original Python example: https://github.com/TVCache/TVCache .
- Sandbox/snapshot side: https://github.com/bhaskar792/container-manager-public (Bhaskar; pairs with selective snapshot/fork in the paper).
- Inference is separate: vLLM (https://vllm.ai) on NERSC; TVCache is a tool-value / trajectory cache, not a KV attention cache.
- Upstream roadmap explicitly lists “Representing parallel tool-calls during transitions” — that is the C/D gap this project targets.
